// MeshGuard Host Agent protocol, v1 (P3-T01; master plan §11.1, §11.5, ADR-05).
//
// The Host Agent is the ONLY component with the Docker socket: it is equivalent to root on the host (R-15). It
// therefore accepts closed, typed, declarative parameters only:
//
//   - no request carries a command, a path, a mount, a capability, an image name, a network name or a YAML/JSON
//     document to execute; the agent derives every path from instance_id (/opt/meshguard/tenants/<instance_id>)
//     and every Docker name from slug (project and network mg-t-<slug>, container mg-hs-<slug>, alias hs-<slug>);
//   - an image is a digest that must be in the agent's own allowlist (generated from versions.lock, not writable by
//     the worker); the agent maps it to the repository;
//   - run_uid, net_cidr and the optional fallback STUN port must lie in the host's locally configured ranges;
//   - before touching an existing directory, network or container the agent checks that it belongs to the same
//     instance (meta/instance.json, labels meshguard.instance_id / meshguard.tenant_id) — never adopts;
//   - a field the agent does not know (unknown field, unknown enum value) is a refusal, never ignored.
//
// Transport: gRPC over the Unix socket /run/meshguard/agent.sock (host: /opt/meshguard/run/agent.sock), no TCP.
// Every call is authenticated twice: the kernel-attested peer credentials (SO_PEERCRED, worker UID allowlist) and
// the agent token (metadata "authorization: Bearer <token>", a file secret). A refusal is a gRPC status
// (INVALID_ARGUMENT, FAILED_PRECONDITION, NOT_FOUND, ABORTED, UNAUTHENTICATED, PERMISSION_DENIED) carrying one
// Refusal detail (reason + field path, never the refused value).
//
// Fields marked [debug_redact = true] carry secrets: never log them, nor any message that contains them
// (protobuf-go's String() does not honour debug_redact; the marker is for reviewers and tools that do).

